Certainly! Below is a C++ program that implements the Bubble Sort algorithm to sort an array of integers in ascending order. Bubble Sort is a simple comparison-based sorting algorithm.

```cpp
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

// Function to perform bubble sort
void bubbleSort(int arr[], int n) {
    int i, j, temp;
    for (i = 0; i < n-1; i++) {
        // Last i elements are already in place
        for (j = 0; j < n-i-1; j++) {
            // Swap if the element found is greater than the next element
            if (arr[j] > arr[j+1]) {
                temp = arr[j];
                arr[j] = arr[j+1];
                arr[j+1] = temp;
            }
        }
    }
}

